- scan response: complete local name.

## Advertising API

Declarations:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.h:364-394`

```c
int bt_start_advertising(uint8_t type,
                         FAR const struct bt_eir_s *ad,
                         FAR const struct bt_eir_s *sd);

int bt_stop_advertising(void);
```

`struct bt_eir_s` is:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/include/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_core.h:123-130`

```c
begin_packed_struct struct bt_eir_s
{
  uint8_t len;
  uint8_t type;
  uint8_t data[29];
} end_packed_struct;
```

The `len` field is the AD structure length, including the AD type byte. For example, a 16-bit UUID payload needs:

```c
.len  = 3,                    /* type byte + two UUID bytes */
.type = BT_EIR_UUID16_ALL,
.data = { 0xf0, 0xff }
```

The implementation copies `len + 1` bytes beginning at the `len` field:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.c:2099-2109`

```c
memcpy(&set_data->data[set_data->len], &ad[i], ad[i].len + 1);
set_data->len += ad[i].len + 1;
```

Arrays terminate with an entry whose `.len == 0`.

The implementation limits each advertising or scan-response command to 29 bytes of AD payload:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.c:2103-2105` and `2136-2138`.

It then sends:

1. `LE_SET_ADV_DATA`
2. `LE_SET_SCAN_RSP_DATA`
3. `LE_SET_ADV_PARAMETERS`
4. `LE_SET_ADV_ENABLE`

at:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.c:2088-2176`.

The default advertising interval is hard-coded to 300 units:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/wireless/bluetooth/bt_hcicore.c:2156-2164`

```c
set_param->min_interval = BT_HOST2LE16(300);
set_param->max_interval = BT_HOST2LE16(300);
```

The current implementation does not first stop advertising before programming new data. If replacing the default advertisement after registration, use:

```c
bt_stop_advertising();
bt_start_advertising(...);
```

and handle `-EALREADY` from `bt_stop_advertising()` if the state is not what the board expects.

Nordic has a compile-time advertising capability dependency:

`/home/mi/vela_competition/contest/nuttx/arch/arm/src/nrf53/nrf53_sdc.c:109-114`

Advertising requires `CONFIG_NRF53_SDC_ADVERTISING` and a nonzero peripheral count. Otherwise the board may register successfully but the controller configuration will not support the advertising commands.

